Z||000011||FieroKyle||07-17-2001||11:29 PM||||HaHa, I have this problem. I live in a town of like 4,000, not a huge town. And if ya drive a car through are town enough and frequently, the cops know who drives what after a while. Well they seem to think me in a black sports car with lisence plate TICKET and me being 16 and all is really funny. There are only 3 cop cars and about maybe 8 cops in our town. So it isn't really overstaffed and many people know eachother. But yeah they follow me all the time. No tickets yet, have came close though. =)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg">  <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>AOL Name: Yakty Yak<BR>E-Mail: YaktyYak@aol.com<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||My7Fieros||07-18-2001||01:19 AM||||Somebody said something about cops seeing sports cars and thinking "ticket"...nahhh.<BR>The agency I work for most everyone drives some sort of sports car...Mustang, Camaro, ect (Fiero for myself of course).<BR>My friend works for another agency (Memphis Police Dept) and I swear you look at the parking lot there and there are more Corvettes (my friend drives one to) and Mustangs than you could ever imagine.<BR>"Sports car = ticket"? Nahhhh<BR>(You <I>really</I> didnt think I would pass up this topic did ya?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||4
